/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 70 0 R
/E (By 2050, agriculture must produce 50% more food, yet pests already destroy up to 40% of crops and cause more than $220 billion in annual losses. Climate change is expanding pest ranges, while chemical controls drive resistance, toxic residue accumulation and severe ecological damage through non-target effects. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
